From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: default AP GRO off for native QCA PPE

The native PPE WLAN ingress hook accepts MTU-sized packets. GRO aggregates
skip that hook and leave most uploads in software. Disable AP GRO when the
interface opens on platforms with native QCA PPE; retain normal TC and
netfilter ordering, station GRO and Ethernet features.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/net/mac80211/iface.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/iface.c
@@ -1373,6 +1373,16 @@ int ieee80211_do_open(struct wireless_de
 
 	lockdep_assert_wiphy(local->hw.wiphy);
 
+	/*
+	 * Native PPE ingress accepts MTU-sized frames. Keep AP RX unaggregated
+	 * by default; the ordinary TC/netfilter receive path still runs.
+	 */
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_QCOM_80211AX_PPE) && dev &&
+	    sdata->vif.type == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP) {
+		dev->wanted_features &= ~NETIF_F_GRO;
+		netdev_update_features(dev);
+	}
+
 	switch (sdata->vif.type) {
 	case NL80211_IFTYPE_AP_VLAN: {
 		struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *master;
